\(E[X] = p\) and \(\operatorname{Var}(X) = p(1-p)\).
This is the Bernoulli distribution, and it is the atom the first half of this unit is built from. Note that the variance is largest at \(p = 0.5\) and vanishes at \(p = 0\) or \(1\): a coin you cannot predict is the most variable one there is.

